 4. 🌺 1 for the road: Inside the Smithsonian&#x27;s holiday workshop 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Over a thousand poinsettias ready for their holiday debut at Smithsonian Gardens. Photo: Anna Spiegel/Axios Axios D.C.'s Anna Spiegel recently got a rare behind-the-scenes tour of Smithsonian Gardens' greenhouses in Suitland, Maryland.

 🎄 Christmas starts in April at the Smithsonian, when the team orders poinsettias for the coming holidays.

 Tiny rooted cuttings arrive around the Fourth of July. Over the next five months, they're watered, fertilized and pruned into showstoppers. Come September, it's lights out: Poinsettias need more than 12 hours of uninterrupted darkness to develop. Horticulturalist Jill Gonzalez hand-ties each poinsettia. Photo: Anna Spiegel/Axios Each museum gets its own holiday look.

 Air and Space goes for celestial themes, while Natural History favors pink poinsettias. American History? Classic Christmas red. Go deeper ... Get Axios Local . 

 
 
